  "rounds": {
    "1": {
      "note": "Hotel vocabulary leans toward the formal end of Cantonese — it lives in service contexts. <em>zau2 dim3</em> (酒店) is the standard word for hotel. Expect the receptionist to ask <em>nei5 deng6 zo2 fong2 mei6 aa3?</em> ('have you booked?'). The verbs <strong>jap6 zyu6</strong> (入住, check in, literally 'enter and stay') and <strong>teoi3 fong2</strong> (退房, check out, 'return room') are compound expressions worth learning whole.",
      "words": [
